  "study_notes": {
    "observed": "Job Corps field survey photos (<=2018-09, p.279): from the NW, the green standing-seam gable roof of the gym hall with dark green walls and a clerestory row under the NNW eave, the white drum with a slanted glazed top on the NNW footprint arc, the lower white flat-roofed annex with roof plant and the hall gable above it at the WSW end; from the SW, the annex WSW end (grey concrete NNW part with a red door, cream SSE part with a gridded window and a dark recessed corner entry) and, partly, the hall SSE eave side (green walls, clerestory).",
    "inferred": "Hall eave height, roof pitch and clerestory cadence; drum height and glazing slope; annex height; stations of the door, window and corner entry. The hall SSE clerestory follows the partial SSE view. The unphotographed ENE strip, annex SSE face and hall ENE gable are plain walls (owner rule); the photographed WSW porch and red door are the entrances.",
    "footprint": "Frozen ring split into the convex gym hall (gable ridge along e9), the WSW annex, the NNW drum cap (mono roof) and the ENE strip."
  }
